{"name":"Polished Concrete","hex":"#9e9793","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"polished","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made smooth or shiny by polishing.","Refined, elegant."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of polish"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/polished"},{"term":"concrete","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Real, actual, tangible.","Analogous to the categories of algebraic objects which category theory was created to generalize, in the sense of having objects which can be thought of as sets equipped with some additional structure. Formally, equipped with a faithful functor to the category of sets."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A building material created by mixing cement, water, and aggregate such as gravel and sand.","Such a material whose cement is Portland cement or a similar limestone derivative."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/concrete"}],"entries":[{"title":"Polished concrete","blocks":[{"text":"Polished concrete is a concrete floor which has been mechanically ground, honed and polished with bonded abrasives in order to achieve a desired level of sheen or gloss."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/Polished_Concrete_Floor.jpg/330px-Polished_Concrete_Floor.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Polished_concrete","wikidata":"Q794236"},{"title":"Polishing","blocks":[{"text":"Polishing is the process of creating a smooth and shiny surface by rubbing it or by applying a chemical treatment, leaving a clean surface with a significant specular reflection. In some materials, polishing is also able to reduce diffuse reflection to minimal values."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Polishing","wikidata":"Q1054722"},{"title":"Concrete","blocks":[{"text":"Concrete is a composite material composed of aggregate bound together with 