on_%28Rome%29_-_Dome.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/Pantheon_%28Rome%29_-_Dome.jpg/1280px-Pantheon_%28Rome%29_-_Dome.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/Pantheon_%28Rome%29_-_Dome.jpg/500px-Pantheon_%28Rome%29_-_Dome.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Interior of the Pantheon dome, seen from beneath. The concrete for the coffered dome was laid on moulds, mounted on temporary scaffolding.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APantheon_(Rome)_-_Dome.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Museo_Foro_Caesaragusta_-_Cloaca_del_foro_03.JPG/500px-Museo_Foro_Caesaragusta_-_Cloaca_del_foro_03.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Museo_Foro_Caesaragusta_-_Cloaca_del_foro_03.JPG/1280px-Museo_Foro_Caesaragusta_-_Cloaca_del_foro_03.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Museo_Foro_Caesaragusta_-_Cloaca_del_foro_03.JPG/500px-Museo_Foro_Caesaragusta_-_Cloaca_del_foro_03.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Opus caementicium exposed in a characteristic Roman arch. In contrast to modern concrete structures, the concrete used in Roman buildings was usually covered with brick or stone.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMuseo_Foro_Caesaragusta_-_Cloaca_del_foro_03.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/61/Smeaton%27s_Lighthouse00.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/61/Smeaton%27s_Lighthouse00.jpg?utm_source